eshow/136039466.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T03:33:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dhananjay Mahapatra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136039567,imgsize-325742.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[First regular India-Nepal passenger train to link birthplaces of Lord Ram and Mata Sita]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/first-regular-india-nepal-passenger-train-to-link-birthplaces-of-lord-ram-and-mata-sita/articleshow/136039011.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136039011.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Indian railways is set to launch a direct passenger train service between Ayodhya and Janakpur after two years. This new connection will promote religious tourism by linking Lord Ram's and Mata Sita's birthplaces. The inaugural run is scheduled for November 23, with the train operating weekly. Passengers will travel around 604 kilometers in approximately 19 hours with customs clearance aboard.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/first-regular-india-nepal-passenger-train-to-link-birthplaces-of-lord-ram-and-mata-sita/articleshow/136039011.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/first-regular-india-nepal-passenger-train-to-link-birthplaces-of-lord-ram-and-mata-sita/articleshow/136039011.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T02:06:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136039019,imgsize-96974.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Don't reduce it to bilateral': Pakistan minister in Delhi for SCO ducks question on terror]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-reduce-it-to-bilateral-pakistan-minister-in-delhi-for-sco-ducks-question-on-terror/articleshow/136035114.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136035114.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Musadik Masood Malik, the Pakistani minister, participated in the SCO Civilisational Dialogue Forum in New Delhi. He acknowledged India's suffering from terror attacks while avoiding direct questions about terror networks in Pakistan. Malik emphasized the importance of an evidence-based mechanism to address terrorism and restore trust between the countries. He advocated for regional cooperation rather than focusing solely on bilateral disputes between India and Pakistan.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-reduce-it-to-bilateral-pakistan-minister-in-delhi-for-sco-ducks-question-on-terror/articleshow/136035114.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-reduce-it-to-bilateral-pakistan-minister-in-delhi-for-sco-ducks-question-on-terror/articleshow/136035114.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T22:51:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136035159,imgsize-66332.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NIA probes 'Indian footprint' in flydubai pilot stabbing case, seeks UAE assistance]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nia-probes-indian-footprint-in-flydubai-pilot-stabbing-case-seeks-uae-assistance/articleshow/136034658.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136034658.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The National Investigation Agency is currently probing the shocking mid-air stabbing of Captain Smit Machchhar, where an Omani first officer allegedly attempted to hijack a flydubai flight. Authorities are now exploring any possible Indian links to the suspect. Additionally, they've sent a request for legal assistance to the UAE to secure important documents while delving into the deeper conspiracy surrounding this alarming incident.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nia-probes-indian-footprint-in-flydubai-pilot-stabbing-case-seeks-uae-assistance/articleshow/136034658.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nia-probes-indian-footprint-in-flydubai-pilot-stabbing-case-seeks-uae-assistance/articleshow/136034658.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T22:38:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136034758,imgsize-783031.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Voice of every village': Rahul attacks BJP after Congress's Rajasthan panchayat poll gains]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/voice-of-every-village-rahul-attacks-bjp-after-congresss-rajasthan-panchayat-poll-gains/articleshow/136034419.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136034419.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/voice-of-every-village-rahul-attacks-bjp-after-congresss-rajasthan-panchayat-poll-gains/articleshow/136034419.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/voice-of-every-village-rahul-attacks-bjp-after-congresss-rajasthan-panchayat-poll-gains/articleshow/136034419.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T22:37:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kanchan Yadav</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136034755,imgsize-42488.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ex-IAF vice-chief slams UK report claiming India has 32 Rafales instead of 36 as 'patently false']]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ex-iaf-vice-chief-slams-uk-report-claiming-india-has-32-rafales-instead-of-36-as-patently-false/articleshow/136032707.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136032707.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ex-iaf-vice-chief-slams-uk-report-claiming-india-has-32-rafales-instead-of-36-as-patently-false/articleshow/136032707.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ex-iaf-vice-chief-slams-uk-report-claiming-india-has-32-rafales-instead-of-36-as-patently-false/articleshow/136032707.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T21:38:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Surendra Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136032952,imgsize-162911.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Government hails growing trust as US navy vessel undergoes repair in India]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/government-hails-growing-trust-as-us-navy-vessel-undergoes-repair-in-india/articleshow/136032711.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136032711.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/government-hails-growing-trust-as-us-navy-vessel-undergoes-repair-in-india/articleshow/136032711.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/government-hails-growing-trust-as-us-navy-vessel-undergoes-repair-in-india/articleshow/136032711.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T21:38:04+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136032937,imgsize-100402.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Government avoids war of words, fears extradition push is a delaying tactic]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/government-avoids-war-of-words-fears-extradition-push-is-a-delaying-tactic/articleshow/136031685.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136031685.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Bangladesh's Prime Minister Tarique Rahman has leveled serious allegations at India and the Awami League, previously led by Sheikh Hasina, suggesting they are stoking discord. The Indian government refrains from offering comments, emphasizing its commitment to fostering a positive relationship with Bangladesh. Furthermore, concerns arise over Hasina's passport application, which Dhaka rejected amid concerns regarding its authenticity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/government-avoids-war-of-words-fears-extradition-push-is-a-delaying-tactic/articleshow/136031685.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/government-avoids-war-of-words-fears-extradition-push-is-a-delaying-tactic/articleshow/136031685.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T21:10:38+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136032212,imgsize-101808.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pahalgam attack: Beijing yet to share info on how GoPro camera US supplied to China was found on terrorists]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pahalgam-attack-beijing-yet-to-share-info-on-how-gopro-camera-us-supplied-to-china-were-found-on-terrorists/articleshow/136031503.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136031503.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pahalgam-attack-beijing-yet-to-share-info-on-how-gopro-camera-us-supplied-to-china-were-found-on-terrorists/articleshow/136031503.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pahalgam-attack-beijing-yet-to-share-info-on-how-gopro-camera-us-supplied-to-china-were-found-on-terrorists/articleshow/136031503.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T20:41:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136031569,imgsize-262552.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['No complaint in Tihar': NIA chief rejects US citizen VanDyke's claim of torture in jail]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-complaint-in-tihar-nia-chief-rejects-us-citizen-vandykes-claim-of-torture-in-jail/articleshow/136031053.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136031053.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Mathew VanDyke, an American citizen, has accused Indian authorities of custodial torture during his time in Tihar jail. Despite the National Investigation Agency (NIA) chief asserting that VanDyke did not report any mistreatment while in judicial custody, he was arrested alongside six Ukrainians for allegedly training insurgents in Myanmar and unlawfully entering India.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-complaint-in-tihar-nia-chief-rejects-us-citizen-vandykes-claim-of-torture-in-jail/articleshow/136031053.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-complaint-in-tihar-nia-chief-rejects-us-citizen-vandykes-claim-of-torture-in-jail/articleshow/136031053.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T20:37:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136031505,imgsize-37086.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Compromised' PM remark: BJP hits back at Rahul Gandhi with AI image of LoP serving water to Trump]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/compromised-pm-remark-bjp-hits-back-at-rahul-gandhi-with-ai-image-of-lop-serving-water-to-trump/articleshow/136029752.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136029752.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Amidst the backdrop of political tensions, BJP spokesperson Gaurav Bhatia fired back at Rahul Gandhi's criticisms about India's lack of representation at the SCO summit with an AI-generated image. Gandhi's remarks targeted Prime Minister Modi's absence, leading BJP officials to highlight India's proactive engagement in international gatherings like BRICS and G20, while scrutinizing the previous Congress-led government's foreign relations strategy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/compromised-pm-remark-bjp-hits-back-at-rahul-gandhi-with-ai-image-of-lop-serving-water-to-trump/articleshow/136029752.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/compromised-pm-remark-bjp-hits-back-at-rahul-gandhi-with-ai-image-of-lop-serving-water-to-trump/articleshow/136029752.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T20:30:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136031324,imgsize-152120.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Partnership will define 21st century': US ambassador Sergio Gor]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/partnership-will-define-21st-century-us-ambassador-sergio-gor/articleshow/136030995.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136030995.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[During his recent visit to the USS George Washington, US Ambassador Sergio Gor emphasized the crucial defense partnership between India and the US, predicting it will shape the 21st century for both nations. Highlighting President Donald Trump's commitment, Gor pointed to advancements in technology access and military training for India, alongside joint military exercises that showcase increasing interoperability and strategic ties.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/partnership-will-define-21st-century-us-ambassador-sergio-gor/articleshow/136030995.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/partnership-will-define-21st-century-us-ambassador-sergio-gor/articleshow/136030995.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T20:20:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136031045,imgsize-54840.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rajasthan panchayat election results 2026: 5 takeaways as Congress beats BJP; RLP makes big gains]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rajasthan-panchayat-election-results-2026-5-takeaways-as-congress-beats-bjp-rlp-makes-big-gains/articleshow/136030091.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136030091.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In the 2026 Rajasthan panchayat elections, Congress emerged victorious, securing thousands of seats and highlighting its political strength. The BJP, on the other hand, faced significant setbacks in key regions, raising questions about its grassroots appeal. Additionally, the Rashtriya Loktantrik Party's gains signify a shifting political landscape, while independent candidates' wins hint at emerging local dynamics. Overall, the results pose serious challenges for the BJP as assembly elections approach.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rajasthan-panchayat-election-results-2026-5-takeaways-as-congress-beats-bjp-rlp-makes-big-gains/articleshow/136030091.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rajasthan-panchayat-election-results-2026-5-takeaways-as-congress-beats-bjp-rlp-makes-big-gains/articleshow/136030091.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T19:52:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pallavi</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136030376,imgsize-65294.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Will put him out of circulation': NIA chief welcomes Canada naming Goldy Brar most-wanted criminal]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/will-put-him-out-of-circulation-nia-chief-welcomes-canada-naming-goldy-brar-most-wanted-criminal/articleshow/136030092.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136030092.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Canadian government has put a $250,000 bounty on gangster Satinderjeet Singh, known as Goldy Brar, who is wanted for first-degree murder connected to a recent homicide in Winnipeg. Brar, who is also on the FBI's Top 10 Most Wanted list with a whopping $1 million reward, poses a serious threat as he is armed and dangerous. His capture would significantly aid ongoing investigations into organized crime activities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/will-put-him-out-of-circulation-nia-chief-welcomes-canada-naming-goldy-brar-most-wanted-criminal/articleshow/136030092.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/will-put-him-out-of-circulation-nia-chief-welcomes-canada-naming-goldy-brar-most-wanted-criminal/articleshow/136030092.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T19:45:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc